    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with a potent lineup anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, who leads the team with a robust 82.62 efficiency score against Kumar Rocker. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from the #1 spot in the lineup and a solid platoon advantage, making him our primary engine for runs and power. Behind him, we see elite upside in the outfield: **Andy Pages** (75.64) and **Kyle Tucker** (75.13) both exploit the 4.82 xERA of Eduardo Rodriguez. **Andy Pages** is particularly intriguing as his score is boosted by the opponent's slow delivery, creating a high-probability environment for stolen bases, a vital component for our 5x5 strategy. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) also earns a strong recommendation, as he faces a soft matchup against Grant Holmes, with his score elevated by both a favorable park shift and a high-upside platoon split.\n\nThe decision to bench **Sam Antonacci** was the most difficult of the morning. While his projected score of 47.36 is respectable, he ultimately fell short due to a suboptimal L/L platoon matchup against Joey Cantillo, which acted as a drag on his efficiency. Conversely, the optimizer favored **Nasim Nunez** (60.32) and **Jacob Wilson** (61.63) for their ability to provide more reliable production in the middle infield. We are keeping a close eye on the official lineups; while the team is currently modeled on projected positions, any shift for **Drake Baldwin** or **Miguel Vargas** out of their premium batting order spots could force a downward adjustment in their output expectations. **Luis Robert Jr.** remains on the bench for today's contest, as his matchup against the elite Jared Jones (3.50 xERA) and a poor platoon outlook render him a liability when we have superior high-efficiency options available.",
